><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-fam=
ily:&quot;Aptos&quot;,sans-serif">If conditions [2] - [4] are met, then USM=
L IV should not apply to the rocket engine you=E2=80=99ve described, and th=
e engine and its parts should be EAR99.&nbsp; If any of these conditions ca=
nnot be met, then the parts could be subject to USML IV(h) and a license wo=
uld be necessary.&nbsp; I don=E2=80=99t believe that=E2=80=99s the case wit=
h this.&nbsp; But it=E2=80=99s good to be careful when working with rockets=
 (in many ways).<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D=
